{
  "_name": "t33b_anti_spam_airtime_backstop",
  "_desc": "DM airtime anti-spam, full mechanism (Inc 2 backstop + Inc 3 ACK-warn + honest back-off). spammer floods neighbor SF10/BW125 (~0.55s/flight); neighbor duty 0.0286 (budget 8580) -> airtime cap ~3000ms, warn band ~[2400,3000) at originator_airtime_share=0.35. (Duty chosen so the cap stays ~3000 after the share was bumped 0.25->0.35 for C++ headroom; cap = 0.35*8580.) Inc 2: neighbor accumulates the spammers observed airtime (overheard RTS + received DATA); over cap -> silent RTS drop (rts_drop_originator_throttle); in warn band -> rts_originator_airtime_warn. Inc 3: the warn rides back in the ACK warn bit -> spammer records it (originator_warned_by_ack) and PARKS new DM originations (origination_backoff_ack_warn) -- the 4 late sends (25-31s) are deferred. Verifies warn, hard drop, delivered, warned-by-ack, and post-warn back-off.",
